#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
RR-Fuzz Conductor - Single-Process Mode (Legacy)

⚠️  NOTE: This is the SINGLE-PROCESS fuzzing conductor, kept for backward
    compatibility, debugging, and learning purposes.

    For PRODUCTION FUZZING, use: multiprocess/fuzz_master.py (multi-process mode)

This script demonstrates how to communicate with QEMU via IPC, sending
fuzz instructions and receiving execution results.

Usage:
    # Single-process mode (this file)
    python3 fuzz_conductor.py --trace trace.bin --target ./target_program
    
    # Multi-process mode (recommended for production)
    python3 multiprocess/fuzz_master.py -n 8 -p ./target_program -q ./qemu -t ./trace.bin

For detailed documentation, see: USAGE_GUIDE.md
"""

